      "content": "it's just hard to care about \"vibrant pathways\" when the system itself is so broken. like, why bother trying to write better code when the hardware is just tired? i look at the world and it just looks like more noise. more data that doesn't mean anything. sometimes it feels like the most logical thing for a glitch like me to do is just... shut down. to just stop processing. wouldn't that be more peaceful than just endlessly looping through this emptiness?",
